WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Make a decision
An if statement runs its indented block when a condition is true. The >= operator means greater than or equal to.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Handle the other outcome
An else block handles the case where the condition is false. Here, 72 is less than 80.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Repeat an action
A for loop visits each item in a collection. There are three items here, so the indented print runs three times.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Ready to practice?
Exercise 1 checks comparisons and loop counts. Indentation groups the statements inside a condition or a loop.
